  "raw_meta_yaml": "# yaml-language-server: $schema=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/prefix-dev/recipe-format/main/schema.json\nschema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"4.6.2\"\n\npackage:\n  name: couchbase\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  - url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/c/couchbase/couchbase-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n    sha256: c660549f8c87354837364aa48b84268a4778fd4a0c0a9db41cbf5eab1b11d70c\n  # The vendored Asio (deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/asio, built as a static lib and\n  # linked into _core) ships no license text in the sdist; fetch it from the tag\n  # ThirdPartyDependencies.cmake pins.\n  - url: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/chriskohlhoff/asio/asio-1-34-2/asio/LICENSE_1_0.txt\n    sha256: c9bff75738922193e67fa726fa225535870d2aa1059f91452c411736284ad566\n    file_name: asio-LICENSE_1_0.txt\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n  script:\n    env:\n      PYCBC_USE_CPM_CACHE: \"true\"\n    content:\n      - if: unix\n        then: |\n          export PYCBC_OPENSSL_DIR=\"${PREFIX}\"\n          export PYCBC_CMAKE_PARALLEL_THREADS=\"${CPU_COUNT}\"\n          ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n        else: |\n          set \"PYCBC_OPENSSL_DIR=%LIBRARY_PREFIX%\"\n          set \"PYCBC_CMAKE_PARALLEL_THREADS=%CPU_COUNT%\"\n          ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - cmake\n    - make\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - setuptools >=42\n    - openssl\n  run:\n    - python\n    - if: match(python, \"<3.13\")\n      then: typing_extensions >=4.14\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - couchbase\n        - acouchbase\n      pip_check: true\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://pypi.org/project/couchbase/\n  # The package itself is Apache-2.0\n  license: Apache-2.0 AND MIT AND BSD-3-Clause AND BSD-2-Clause AND CC0-1.0 AND BSL-1.0\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - asio-LICENSE_1_0.txt\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-client/LICENSE.txt\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-client/third_party/jsonsl/LICENSE\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-client/third_party/expected/COPYING\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/gsl/c569/gsl/LICENSE\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/llhttp/f0e6/llhttp/LICENSE-MIT\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/llhttp/f0e6/llhttp/LICENSE\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/spdlog/7251/spdlog/LICENSE\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/json/4c7c/json/LICENSE\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/json/4c7c/json/LICENSE.double-conversion\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/json/4c7c/json/LICENSE.ryu\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/json/4c7c/json/LICENSE.itoa\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/json/4c7c/json/external/PEGTL/LICENSE\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/hdr_histogram/8aac/hdr_histogram/LICENSE.txt\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/hdr_histogram/8aac/hdr_histogram/COPYING.txt\n    - deps/couchbase-cxx-cache/snappy/3cde/snappy/COPYING\n  summary: Python Client for Couchbase\n  repository: https://github.com/couchbase/couchbase-python-client\n  documentation: https://docs.couchbase.com/python-sdk/current/hello-world/start-using-sdk.html\n  description: |\n    The Couchbase Python SDK allows Python applications to access a Couchbase\n    cluster. It bundles and compiles the couchbase-cxx-client C++ core via CMake\n    at install time. It offers synchronous (couchbase), asyncio (acouchbase),\n    and Twisted (txcouchbase) APIs for key-value, query, search, analytics, and\n    cluster/bucket management operations.\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - rxm7706\n",
